# The script the set's fixture harness runs stepped (`fixture-test`, through
# tools/package-set.sh; docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate
# runs a fixture") against
# the config in `config/`, to list a binding of config's in the binding
# search (`search-bindings`), to run it through the search, and to run a
# command of config's that names a declaration of the search's module. What
# it prints must be exactly `expected`. It touches no file.

reload
settle

# `search-bindings`, called with no text, asks `Binding: ` with every
# binding the scheme reaches as its candidates. Config's style `starts`
# keeps those the text starts: with `SPC y` typed, config's binding, its
# keys, its command and its description, `SPC y y  yy-said  Say it`.
run search-bindings
commit SPC y
scene

# Accepting runs the binding as its key would: `yy-said` says `said` in the
# echo area.
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# Config's command that names `BindingSearch.label` says the search's label
# in the echo area: config reaches the binding search's module.
run search-label
scene
